license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >
  Planned Lean 4 formalization of the Interpretive Kernel of Structural
  Explainability. The theory investigates how equivalence relations
  on distinct carriers are related through explicit interpretations
  and comparison rules. Its proposed scope includes finite equivalence
  and partition structures, interpretation-induced kernels, refinement
  and admissibility conditions, coherent output regimes, threshold
  constructions, and finite witnesses of incompatibility or
  incomparability. The objective is to characterize the mathematical
  conditions under which interpretations preserve or distinguish
  declared relationships without presupposing agreement about domain
  meaning. The repository does not define domain semantics, operational
  audits, or the identity-regime taxonomy.

keywords:
